# what sdk/cgo/compose.sh lays here and records, and what a library build writes
/.composed
/build/

# THE COMPOSED FILES: the core SDK's cgo package main, as compose.sh copies it from the core SDK at
# the commit scripts/siblings.txt pins. They are the core's source, laid here for a build and removed
# by `compose.sh --clean`, so a `git add -A` in a composed tree must not commit them. compose.sh
# holds this list to what it copied, both ways: a core that gains or loses a file fails the compose
# until the list here says so.
# composed-begin
/callbacks.c
/callbacks.h
/convert.go
/cstrings.go
/exports_core.go
/exports_gen.go
/exports_gen_unix.go
/exports_manual.go
/exports_socket.go
/handles.go
/include/urnetwork_sdk.h
/include/urnetwork_sdk.hpp
# composed-end
